-- Black Alibi MM2 | stable release
-- version : 1.0.2
-- author  : by GachiRave
-- target  : Murder Mystery 2
--
-- how roles are read (no waiting for the 10s role selector):
--   1. GetPlayerData, requested once when the script starts
--   2. Fade / UpdatePlayerData events sent by MM2
--   3. equipment, only as a silent fallback
-- hero is layered on top: the round's sheriff is remembered from the
-- data, and any other player holding the gun afterwards is painted Hero
--
-- ============================================================
-- CHANGELOG 1.0.2
-- ============================================================
-- ADDED
--   Server Hop on the Teleport tab. Pulls the public server list, drops any
--   server that is full or the one you are already in, and jumps to a random
--   survivor. Falls back to a same-place rejoin if the list can't be read.
--
--   Teleport To Sheriff and Teleport To Murderer. Both read the role table
--   built by the role engine and drop you right behind the target: one stud
--   for the sheriff, roughly two and a half for the murderer, close enough
--   for a clean revolver shot without walking into melee range.
--
--   Murderer Radar on the ESP tab. A compass arrow plus a distance readout
--   that tracks the murderer's position through walls once their role is
--   known, so you always know which way to run.
--
--   Danger Alert on the ESP tab. Pulses a red screen border and fires a
--   notification the moment the murderer closes inside eighteen studs.
--
--   Auto Collect Coins on the Extra tab. Touches every coin inside a short
--   radius on its own, no more manual sweeping of the map.
--
--   Role Reveal banner. The instant the round hands you a role, a card
--   slides down from the top of the screen with your role name and colour,
--   then clears itself after four seconds.
--
--   Knife Throw button for the murderer. Turning it on drops a draggable
--   button onto the screen; tapping it drives the knife into the nearest
--   clear target, preferring the sheriff whenever one is out in the open,
--   and the same line of sight check used by the aimbot keeps it from
--   firing through walls.
--
-- FIXED
--   Kill All could bring the whole client down on a full lobby. The sweep
--   now runs on frame synced waits instead of raw timers, re-validates the
--   knife and every target before each touch, and never touches a torn
--   reference left behind by a player who disconnected mid sweep.
--
-- CHANGED
--   Prediction Aimbot now solves its own lead time in two passes instead of
--   one, closing the gap that under led targets sprinting across the screen.
--
--   Toggle rows and panel switches get a short press and release scale plus
--   a small bounce on their ON / OFF pill, matching the buttons that already
--   had that feedback.
--
--   Window height grew to fit the new controls without crowding the tabs
--   that were already there.
-- ============================================================
-- CHANGELOG 1.0.1
-- ============================================================
-- ADDED
--   Prediction Aimbot tracks the murderer's body and calculates horizontal
--   lead from distance, network latency and smoothed assembly velocity.
--   Vertical lead is handled separately and capped to one stud, so a jumping
--   target cannot drag the crosshair several metres into the air.
--
--   Kill All in the murderer panel. One sweep over every living player
--   instead of waiting for them to walk into aura range.
--
--   Auto Grab Gun on the Extra tab. Watches for the drop and collects it
--   automatically, then returns you to the spot you were standing on.
--
-- FIXED
--   Kill Aura range was never written into a config. Saving a preset kept
--   the toggles but the slider always came back as 12. The number is part
--   of the snapshot now and is restored on load.
--
--   Line of sight could still approve a target behind thin or one sided
--   geometry, so the aim sometimes locked through a wall. The check now
--   samples the head, torso and lower body, and any solid hit blocks it.
--
-- CHANGED
--   Renamed from Black Alibi GachiRave to Black Alibi MM2.
--   Page transitions, toggle feedback and notification motion reworked.
-- ============================================================

